  "description": "Republic of Ireland District Electoral Divisions/Wards as at 1971-04-15, assembled from Connacht (= 1957 boundaries), Leinster 1971, Munster 1971, Ulster (= 1963 boundaries). Modified version of District Electoral Divisions/Wards 1977. In 1977, due to the expansion of Drogheda, part of the DED of St. Mary’s was ceded to County Louth by County Meath. Details on this can be found in the Local Government Provisional Order Confirmation Act, 1976. Also relevant is the renaming of An Uaimh to Navan on 25 Jun 1971, as its corresponding DEDs were renamed by 1971 Census Reports Volume 1 (published July 1972).",
